[{:db/id 17592186152157 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-599b6849-3342-5594-bc18-d66421f45e91"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-599b6849-3342-5594-bc18-d66421f45e91" :question/id #uuid "599b6849-3342-5594-bc18-d66421f45e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-75983" :question/problem "The matrix $Q$ is given below. Let ${q}_{1}$, ${q}_{2}$,  ${q}_{3}$ and ${q}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $Q.$
Determine if $B=\text{{}{q}_{1},{q}_{4}\text{}}$ is a basis of $\text{Col}(Q).$ 
If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${q}_{3}={x}_{1}{q}_{1}+{x}_{4}{q}_{4}.$ 

$$
Q=[\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -30 & -15 \\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\ 4 & 0 & 24 & 14\end{aligned}]
$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $Q$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):

$$
\begin{aligned}Q & =[\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -30 & -15 \\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\ 4 & 0 & 24 & 14\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\  & ∼[\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 3 \\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\ 4 & 0 & 24 & 14\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\  & ∼[\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 3 \\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\  & ∼[\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\  & ∼[\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\end{aligned}]\end{aligned}
$$

From the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns. So, a basis of $\text{Col}(Q)$ is $\{{q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{4}\}.$ 

So, we conclude that $B=\{{q}_{1},{q}_{4}\}$ is not a basis of $\text{Col}(Q).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2cf517a6-abf9-5b4f-942e-0933e5866f68"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2cf517a6-abf9-5b4f-942e-0933e5866f68" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf517a6-abf9-5b4f-942e-0933e5866f68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3bb4d8dd-5f42-53d6-b9ea-b3eb6b57a83a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0dee10fc-3dcb-5237-af24-246152c9267c" "answer-3f53ddd2-bec1-5acd-9379-2bb08043f9b8" "answer-1e13e6c1-1f37-56f8-a726-2aee62b71439" "answer-8e0920b1-977a-544d-8f3c-6269c1d5b48c" "answer-3bb4d8dd-5f42-53d6-b9ea-b3eb6b57a83a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0dee10fc-3dcb-5237-af24-246152c9267c" :answer/id #uuid "0dee10fc-3dcb-5237-af24-246152c9267c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f53ddd2-bec1-5acd-9379-2bb08043f9b8" :answer/id #uuid "3f53ddd2-bec1-5acd-9379-2bb08043f9b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e13e6c1-1f37-56f8-a726-2aee62b71439" :answer/id #uuid "1e13e6c1-1f37-56f8-a726-2aee62b71439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e0920b1-977a-544d-8f3c-6269c1d5b48c" :answer/id #uuid "8e0920b1-977a-544d-8f3c-6269c1d5b48c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bb4d8dd-5f42-53d6-b9ea-b3eb6b57a83a" :answer/id #uuid "3bb4d8dd-5f42-53d6-b9ea-b3eb6b57a83a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\{{q}_{1},{q}_{4}\}$ is not a basis of $\text{Col}(Q)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-594a47fa-1a44-547a-9d72-e8c6cf9a66a8" :activity/id #uuid "594a47fa-1a44-547a-9d72-e8c6cf9a66a8" :activity/title "Finding a Basis of the Column Space of a Matrix" :activity/type :act