{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$

First, we recall the following  identities:

$$
\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\frac{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\,\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\frac{1}{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}
$$

Now, we rewrite the integral using the above identities, as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{0}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\operatorname{coth}⁡x\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\operatorname{sech}⁡x\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\,\text{d}x & ={\int }_{0}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\frac{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\cdot \operatorname{sinh}⁡x\cdot \frac{1}{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\cdot \operatorname{cosh}⁡x\,\text{d}x \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\,\text{d}x \\  & =\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\,{|}_{0}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\  & =\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\operatorname{sinh}⁡0 \\  & =\frac{{e}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{-\operatorname{ln}⁡3}}{2}-0 \\  & =\frac{3-{3}^{-1}}{2} \\  & =\frac{(\frac{8}{3})}{2} \\  & =\frac{8}{6} \\  & =\frac{4}{3}\end{aligned}
$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c87e6d3b-23bd-5b1e-bec0-bba379741512"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c87e6d3b-23bd-5b1e-bec0-bba379741512" :answer-field/id #uuid "c87e6d3b-23bd-5b1e-bec0-bba379741512" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-25f737d4-4208-55a3-aa88-7222aded4409" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25f737d4-4208-55a3-aa88-7222aded4409"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25f737d4-4208-55a3-aa88-7222aded4409" :answer/id #uuid "25f737d4-4208-55a3-aa88-7222aded4409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f16bf74-fd62-5389-9de5-031fc7e1da5b" :question/id #uuid "5f16bf74-fd62-5389-9de5-031fc7e1da5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-352935" :question/problem "$$

Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.

${\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\frac{\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\,\text{d}x=$
{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$

$$

First, we write the integral as

$$
{\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\frac{\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\text{d}x={\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\cdot \frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\,\text{d}x.
$$

Now we find the hyperbolic identities corresponding to the trigonometric identities 

$$
\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\frac{1}{\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\,\text{ and }\,\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\frac{\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.
$$

Using Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are

$$
\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\frac{1}{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\,\text{ and }\,\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\frac{\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.
$$

Then, we use the above identities to write the integral as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\cdot \frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\,\text{d}x & ={\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡x\,\text{d}x \\  & =-\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x{|}_{\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0} \\  & =-\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡(0)+\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡(\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2) \\  & =\frac{1}{2}(\frac{4}{({e}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2}+{e}^{-\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2})^{2}}-\frac{4}{({e}^{0}+{e}^{0})^{2}}) \\  & =\frac{2}{(1/2+2)^{2}}-\frac{1}{2} \\  & =-\frac{9}{50}\end{aligned}
$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-408af374-202e-561f-90a6-1910a956b51e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-408af374-202e-561f-90a6-1910a956b51e" :answer-field/id #uuid "408af374-202e-561f-90a6-1910a956b51e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-98919bb4-2785-53dd-9466-f9d0288a76cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98919bb4-2785-53dd-9466-f9d0288a76cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98919bb4-2785-53dd-9466-f9d0288a76cc" :answer/id #uuid "98919bb4-2785-53dd-9466-f9d0288a76cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\frac{9}{50}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb7adc98-109e-57e5-9f19-72ef71c8b698" :question/id #uuid "fb7adc98-109e-57e5-9f19-72ef71c8b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-96265" :question/problem "${\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\frac{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\,\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$

$$

First, we write the integral as

$$
{\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\frac{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\,\text{d}x={\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\frac{1}{\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\cdot \frac{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\text{d}x.
$$

Now, we need to find the hyperbolic identities that correspond to the following trigonometric identities: 

$$
\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\frac{1}{\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\,\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\frac{\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\operatorname{sin}⁡x}
$$

Using Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are

$$
\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\frac{1}{\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\,\,\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\frac{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.
$$

Then, we use the above identities to express the integral as

$$
{\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\operatorname{csch}⁡x\operatorname{coth}⁡x\,\text{d}x.
$$

Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\frac{\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\,\text{d}x & ={\int }_{\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\operatorname{csch}⁡x\operatorname{coth}⁡x\,\text{d}x \\  & =-\operatorname{csch}⁡x{|}_{\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\  & =-\operatorname{csch}⁡(\operatorname{ln}⁡4)+\operatorname{csch}⁡(\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\  & =-\frac{2}{{e}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{-\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}+\frac{2}{{e}^{\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\operatorname{ln}⁡2}} \\  & =-\frac{2}{4-{4}^{-1}}+\frac{2}{2-{2}^{-1}} \\  & =-\frac{8}{15}+\frac{4}{3} \\  & =\frac{4}{5}.\end{aligned}
$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f4c241c-0bbe-5dbc-9897-1ee7bd328728"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f4c241c-0bbe-5dbc-9897-1ee7bd328728" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f4c241c-0bbe-5dbc-9897-1ee7bd328728" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-234cc714-ee95-51d3-9f60-96338562378e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f31d1d3-9617-5495-b1c8-0bd332072ade" "answer-529a7029-8e13-5a97-9918-a3b488d2c78c" "answer-fffb787f-ff79-5c83-b983-661bbcea077a" "answer-234cc714-ee95-51d3-9f60-96338562378e" "answer-70329641-1279-5076-9f37-fb06772be638"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f31d1d3-9617-5495-b1c8-0bd332072ade" :answer/id #uuid "4f31d1d3-9617-5495-b1c8-0bd332072ade" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-529a7029-8e13-5a97-9918-a3b488d2c78c" :answer/id #uuid "529a7029-8e13-5a97-9918-a3b488d2c78c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fffb787f-ff79-5c83-b983-661bbcea077a" :answer/id #uuid "fffb787f-ff79-5c83-b983-661bbcea077a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{4}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-234cc714-ee95-51d3-9f60-96338562378e" :answer/id #uuid "234cc714-ee95-51d3-9f60-96338562378e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70329641-1279-5076-9f37-fb06772be638" :answer/id #uuid "70329641-1279-5076-9f37-fb06772be638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-15a967e4-1f67-5afa-8031-c76c4fbb09cf" :question/id #uuid "15a967e4-1f67-5afa-8031-c76c4fbb09cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-96263" :question/problem "$\int \frac{5\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\,\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$

$$

