 :question/math-academy-id "q-154082" :question/problem "The mass $m$ of a tablet PC measures $314.7\,\text{g}$ to the nearest tenth of a gram. Determine the upper and lower bounds of this measurement." :question/worked-solution "Our measurement is given to the nearest $0.1\,\text{g}.$ So, the greatest possible error of this measurement is

$$
\frac{0.1\,\text{g}}{2}=0.05\,\text{g}.
$$

Therefore, we can calculate the lower and upper bounds of this measurement as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}\text{lower bound} & =314.7\,\text{g}-0.05\,\text{g} \\  & =314.65\,\text{g} \\ \text{upper bound} & =314.7\,\text{g}+0.05\,\text{g} \\  & =314.75\,\text{g}\end{aligned}
$$

Since the exact value of $m$ lies between the lower and upper bound, we conclude that

$$
314.65\,\text{g}\le m<314.75\,\text{g}.
$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6435960d-f51a-52e7-94e7-a76e47e9ec99"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6435960d-f51a-52e7-94e7-a76e47e9ec99" :answer-field/id #uuid "6435960d-f51a-52e7-94e7-a76e47e9ec99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-06b7ceac-a5dd-5a5e-81f6-5093daac715f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86ccb7e9-64a7-58a7-9d0c-22ade13bddc2" "answer-06b7ceac-a5dd-5a5e-81f6-5093daac715f" "answer-5237a001-734d-52ba-8325-09127dd19a3d" "answer-334f31b7-f7be-595d-b52c-848908f510f2" "answer-52df3fc4-f30c-5656-9770-f6b6852fee06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86ccb7e9-64a7-58a7-9d0c-22ade13bddc2" :answer/id #uuid "86ccb7e9-64a7-58a7-9d0c-22ade13bddc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "313.7\,\text{g}\le m<315.7\,\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06b7ceac-a5dd-5a5e-81f6-5093daac715f" :answer/id #uuid "06b7ceac-a5dd-5a5e-81f6-5093daac715f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "314.65\,\text{g}\le m<314.75\,\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5237a001-734d-52ba-8325-09127dd19a3d" :answer/id #uuid "5237a001-734d-52ba-8325-09127dd19a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "314.695\,\text{g}\le m<314.705\,\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-334f31b7-f7be-595d-b52c-848908f510f2" :answer/id #uuid "334f31b7-f7be-595d-b52c-848908f510f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "314.69\,\text{g}\le m<314.71\,\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52df3fc4-f30c-5656-9770-f6b6852fee06" :answer/id #uuid "52df3fc4-f30c-5656-9770-f6b6852fee06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "314.6\,\text{g}\le m<314.8\,\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074397 :question/worked-solution "One of the points belonging to the graph is $(10,15).$

