$$
{(\frac{1}{5})}^{3}=\frac{{1}^{3}}{{5}^{3}}
$$

Now, using ${1}^{3}=1$ and ${5}^{3}=125,$ we get

$$
\frac{{1}^{3}}{{5}^{3}}=\frac{1}{125}.
$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ba8ba35a-49bb-57fe-8e35-5eb9d11c64aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ba8ba35a-49bb-57fe-8e35-5eb9d11c64aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba8ba35a-49bb-57fe-8e35-5eb9d11c64aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0a5c6d33-1d35-5904-b068-cc3598e10f87" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0a5c6d33-1d35-5904-b068-cc3598e10f87" "answer-6869578e-010a-5d61-92d2-4038d52299fc" "answer-eb31a0c1-bfa5-5c81-aff5-37d4792278fa" "answer-6420deb4-465e-555a-a374-d785308e82a9" "answer-8cf77517-9738-5543-8399-498bb9e2609f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a5c6d33-1d35-5904-b068-cc3598e10f87" :answer/id #uuid "0a5c6d33-1d35-5904-b068-cc3598e10f87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{1}{125}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6869578e-010a-5d61-92d2-4038d52299fc" :answer/id #uuid "6869578e-010a-5d61-92d2-4038d52299fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{1}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb31a0c1-bfa5-5c81-aff5-37d4792278fa" :answer/id #uuid "eb31a0c1-bfa5-5c81-aff5-37d4792278fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{1}{75}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6420deb4-465e-555a-a374-d785308e82a9" :answer/id #uuid "6420deb4-465e-555a-a374-d785308e82a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{3}{125}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cf77517-9738-5543-8399-498bb9e2609f" :answer/id #uuid "8cf77517-9738-5543-8399-498bb9e2609f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124481 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-05e49986-b987-5b1e-8762-a91ca97898e0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-05e49986-b987-5b1e-8762-a91ca97898e0" :question/id #uuid "05e49986-b987-5b1e-8762-a91ca97898e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-68800" :question/problem "$\sqrt{26}=$" :question/worked-solution "The square root of a product of two positive numbers is equal to the product of the square roots of the numbers. Therefore,

$$
