{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To determine whether the sequence converges or diverges, we need to determine the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:

$$
{lim}_{n\to \infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\to \infty }\frac{12n+1}{3n}.
$$

The dominant term in the denominator is $3n,$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n$ and get

$$
\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\to \infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }\frac{12n+1}{3n} \\  & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }\frac{(\frac{12n}{n}+\frac{1}{n})}{\frac{3n}{n}} \\  & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }\frac{12+\frac{1}{n}}{3} \\  & =\frac{12+0}{3} \\  & =4.\end{aligned}
$$

Consequently, the sequence converges, and its limit is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c43acc61-3f4b-58f8-9442-6e3ef8f460f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c43acc61-3f4b-58f8-9442-6e3ef8f460f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "c43acc61-3f4b-58f8-9442-6e3ef8f460f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ea68bf8b-4deb-5b99-92c1-18ea456b7de6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ea68bf8b-4deb-5b99-92c1-18ea456b7de6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea68bf8b-4deb-5b99-92c1-18ea456b7de6" :answer/id #uuid "ea68bf8b-4deb-5b99-92c1-18ea456b7de6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a4edf402-bea0-5a44-bc5e-8ea032b32554" :activity/id #uuid "a4edf402-bea0-5a44-bc5e-8ea032b32554" :activity/title "Limits of Sequences" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049983 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-06677fb3-7ea6-5165-8cd4-81f9a96fa023" "step-1718a7b4-2d06-538f-8e12-c06876a48a52" "step-662b9fe1-3bf2-5624-8370-6f85b744866a" "step-07528adf-f296-5070-8943-009a2dae445f" "step-55189c97-78f2-5c38-9d2b-e6e0a11aa6ba"] :activity/first-step "step-06677fb3-7ea6-5165-8cd4-81f9a96fa023" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-06677fb3-7ea6-5165-8cd4-81f9a96fa023" :step/id #uuid "06677fb3-7ea6-5165-8cd4-81f9a96fa023" :step/content "question-d26b4fec-f259-5757-943d-c92ed32d5a4b" :step/next "step-1718a7b4-2d06-538f-8e12-c06876a48a52" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1718a7b4-2d06-538f-8e12-c06876a48a52" :step/id #uuid "1718a7b4-2d06-538f-8e12-c06876a48a52" :step/content 17592186416142 :step/next "step-662b9fe1-3bf2-5624-8370-6f85b744866a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-662b9fe1-3bf2-5624-8370-6f85b744866a" :step/id #uuid "662b9fe1-3bf2-5624-8370-6f85b744866a" :step/content 17592186247229 :step/next "step-07528adf-f296-5070-8943-009a2dae445f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-07528adf-f296-5070-8943-009a2dae445f" :step/id #uuid "07528adf-f296-5070-8943-009a2dae445f" :step/content "question-f593ac8e-7a29-5f43-82ff-aea84a5ba69c" :step/next "step-55189c97-78f2-5c38-9d2b-e6e0a11aa6ba" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-55189c97-78f2-5c38-9d2b-e6e0a11aa6ba" :step/id #uuid "55189c97-78f2-5c38-9d2b-e6e0a11aa6ba" :step/content "question-548006ed-ff60-5fe8-9b17-af5147ac7aae" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186051656 :answer-field/choices 17592186051657] [:db/retract 17592186051656 :answer-field/choices 17592186051658] [:db/retract 17592186051656 :answer-field/choices 17592186051659] [:db/retract 17592186051656 :answer-field/choices 17592186051660] [:db/retract 17592186051656 :answer-field/choices 17592186051661] {:db/id 17592186054770 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-60d9e1c1-b611-5995-967c-6c66ed571c82"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-60d9e1c1-b611-5995-967c-6c66ed571c82" :question/id #uuid "60d9e1c1-b611-5995-967c-6c66ed571c82" :question/math-academy-id "q-149565" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-5z\le -1.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $-5.$ To isolate $z,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-5.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.

Also, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:

$$
\begin{aligned}-5z\,\, & \le \,\,-1 \\ \frac{-5z}{-5}\,\, & \ge \,\,\frac{-1}{-5} \\ \frac{-5z}{-5}\,\, & \ge \,\,\frac{1}{5}\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we can cancel a common factor of $-5$ from both the numerator and denominator.

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{-5z}{-5} & \ge \frac{1}{5} \\ \frac{\cancel{-5}z}{\cancel{-5}} & \ge \frac{1}{5} \\ z & \ge \frac{1}{5}\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, the solution is $z\ge \frac{1}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b60c1271-2aa2-5db6-a4fc-0ced692f3cad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b60c1271-2aa2-5db6-a4fc-0ced692f3cad" :answer-field/id #uuid "b60c1271-2aa2-5db6-a4fc-0ced692f3cad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-11e4be9b-77ce-5d2c-870a-9582c9f4eacc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b94c625a-806d-5398-a511-8434b5363807" "answer-91b033fa-0ab3-5c2d-87b8-9809d0825695" "answer-11e4be9b-77ce-5d2c-870a-9582c9f4eacc" "answer-729d4612-b4b3-52d6-a984-56bcadb47c63" "answer-9bb97e3f-8e17-5d53-9ebf-0d14a1a104c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b94c625a-806d-5398-a511-8434b5363807" :answer/id #uuid "b94c625a-806d-5398-a511-8434b5363807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\ge -\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91b033fa-0ab3-5c2d-87b8-9809d0825695" :answer/id #uuid "91b033fa-0ab3-5c2d-87b8-9809d0825695" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\ge 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11e4be9b-77ce-5d2c-870a-9582c9f4eacc" :answer/id #uuid "11e4be9b-77ce-5d2c-870a-9582c9f4eacc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\ge \frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-729d4612-b4b3-52d6-a984-56bcadb47c63" :answer/id #uuid "729d4612-b4b3-52d6-a984-56bcadb47c63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\le -\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bb97e3f-8e17-5d53-9ebf-0d14a1a104c9" :answer/id #uuid "9bb97e3f-8e17-5d53-9ebf-0d14a1a104c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\le \frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054772 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a6005239-b6a4-5801-8173-53f2d74d92ea"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a6005239-b6a4-5801-8173-53f2d74d92ea" :question/id #uuid "a6005239-b6a4-5801-8173-53f2d74d92ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-153600" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4\le x+7.$" :question/worked-solution "To isolate $x,$ we need to perform the *opposite* of *adding* $7,$ which is *subtracting* $7.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.

$$
\begin{aligned}4 & \le x+7 \\ 4-7 & \le x+7-7 \\ -3 & \le x+0 \\ -3 & \le x\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we rewrite the inequality with the variable on the left-hand side:

$$
x\ge -3
$$

Therefore, the solution is $x\ge -3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e410432f-86a4-50ea-8294-40d4d0eeeb2f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e410432f-86a4-50ea-8294-40d4d0eeeb2f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e410432f-86a4-50ea-8294-40d4d0eeeb2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6e12aa20-0d6e-5360-a6c8-7346274c8177" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6e12aa20-0d6e-5360-a6c8-7346274c8177" "answer-6395e4d6-160c-524d-bea0-39d0f0cb0acb" "answer-360ebf0c-440b-5b80-aa5d-f220ea76cfe8" "answer-60e57476-d7c3-5931-afaa-b90f394b253b" "answer-a9e80f2e-a321-5d67-acf6-345376f7ea8f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e12aa20-0d6e-5360-a6c8-7346274c8177" :answer/id #uuid "6e12aa20-0d6e-5360-a6c8-7346274c8177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\ge -3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6395e4d6-160c-524d-bea0-39d0f0cb0acb" :answer/id #uuid "6395e4d6-160c-524d-bea0-39d0f0cb0acb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\ge 11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-360ebf0c-440b-5b80-aa5d-f220ea76cfe8" :answer/id #uuid "360ebf0c-440b-5b80-aa5d-f220ea76cfe8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\ge 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60e57476-d7c3-5931-afaa-b90f394b253b" :answer/id #uuid "60e57476-d7c3-5931-afaa-b90f394b253b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\le -3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9e80f2e-a321-5d67-acf6-345376f7ea8f" :answer/id #uuid "a9e80f2e-a321-5d67-acf6-345376f7ea8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055021 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-\frac{x}{2}\le 4.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $x$ is being *divided* by $2.$ To isolate $x$ and remove the negative sign, we *multiply* by $-2.$ 

Remember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:

$$
\begin{aligned}-\frac{x}{2}\,\, & \le \,\,4 \\ (-2)\cdot (-\frac{x}{2})\,\, & \ge \,\,(-2)\cdot 4 \\ (-2)\cdot (-\frac{x}{2})\,\, & \ge \,\,-8\end{aligned}
$$

Since two negative numbers multiply to give a positive number, we first cancel the negatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}(-2)\cdot (-\frac{x}{2}) & \ge -8 \\ (\cancel{-}2)\cdot (\cancel{-}\frac{x}{2}) & \ge -8 \\ 2\cdot \frac{x}{2} & \ge -8\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we can cancel a common factor of $2$ from both the numerator and denominator.

$$
\begin{aligned}2\cdot \frac{x}{2} & \ge -8 \\ \frac{2x}{2} & \ge -8 \\ \frac{\cancel{2}x}{\cancel{2}} & \ge -8 \\ x & \ge -8\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, the solution is $x\ge -8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186051656 :answer-field/correct "answer-ba590d86-ddb8-598a-a220-46efedf147bc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba590d86-ddb8-598a-a220-46efedf147bc" "answer-55632b59-8ff0-5f33-bd84-759756febdc5" "answer-249f7541-1a8a-52ec-9e0c-a25f296e0698" "answer-e10696b4-01d9-5bd2-8740-a24555a84567" "answer-99888988-7d3e-5baa-ab4a-decbb3967954"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba590d86-ddb8-598a-a220-46efedf147bc" :answer/id #uuid "ba590d86-ddb8-598a-a220-46efedf147bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\ge -8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55632b59-8ff0-5f33-bd84-759756febdc5" :answer/id #uuid "55632b59-8ff0-5f33-bd84-759756febdc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\ge 6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-249f7541-1a8a-52ec-9e0c-a25f296e0698" :answer/id #uuid "249f7541-1a8a-52ec-9e0c-a25f296e0698" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\ge 8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e10696b4-01d9-5bd2-8740-a24555a84567" :answer/id #uuid "e10696b4-01d9-5bd2-8740-a24555a84567" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\le -8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99888988-7d3e-5baa-ab4a-decbb3967954" :answer/id #uuid "99888988-7d3e-5baa-ab4a-decbb3967954" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\le 8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a0296a38-e916-56a7-bb47-0737bade1abd" :activity/id #uuid "a0296a38-e916-56a7-bb47-0737bade1abd" :activity/title "Solving One-Step Linear Inequalities" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049986 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-c4402b05-776a-5423-af2f-f5f1a382df37" "step-c0507717-60f0-50ac-81aa-8044cb88a14c" "step-b48eede8-bb40-5e1b-981b-25334c7cacd0"] :activity/first-step "step-c4402b05-776a-5423-af2f-f5f1a382df37" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/