 resulting point?" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the functional representations of our three transformations:

- A shift of $2$ units up can be represented by the function 

$$
(x,y)↦(x,y+2).
$$

- A reflection in the $y$-axis can be represented by the function 

$$
(x,y)↦(-x,y).
$$

- A shift of $1$ unit to the left can be represented by the function 

$$
(x,y)↦(x-1,y).
$$

Let's apply the given transformations to the point $Q$ using our functions:

First, we apply the shift. The image of the point $(-3,1)$ under the shift is

$$
(-3,1)↦(-3,1+2)=(-3,3).
$$



Then, we apply the reflection. The image of the point $(-3,3)$ under the reflection is

$$
(-3,3)↦(3,3).
$$

Finally, we apply the second shift by $1$ unit to the left. The image of the point $(3,3)$ under the shift is

$$
(3,3)↦(3-1,3)=(2,3).
$$



Therefore, the resulting point is $(2,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4699a690-a8bd-5581-b11e-7163244e6dcf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4699a690-a8bd-5581-b11e-7163244e6dcf" :answer-field/id #uuid "4699a690-a8bd-5581-b11e-7163244e6dcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e044b7d5-8486-58d6-b3fe-085072e21840" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1814799-e689-53a9-80c0-138645ff6068" "answer-a4e5ce62-ea3a-5f89-be1a-a44d806e3912" "answer-3d6aa5e1-96ad-5af2-b67a-d52b21a1d422" "answer-ea7eef76-ed62-5f78-aa7d-5f5fcde472d4" "answer-e044b7d5-8486-58d6-b3fe-085072e21840"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1814799-e689-53a9-80c0-138645ff6068" :answer/id #uuid "d1814799-e689-53a9-80c0-138645ff6068" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4e5ce62-ea3a-5f89-be1a-a44d806e3912" :answer/id #uuid "a4e5ce62-ea3a-5f89-be1a-a44d806e3912" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d6aa5e1-96ad-5af2-b67a-d52b21a1d422" :answer/id #uuid "3d6aa5e1-96ad-5af2-b67a-d52b21a1d422" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea7eef76-ed62-5f78-aa7d-5f5fcde472d4" :answer/id #uuid "ea7eef76-ed62-5f78-aa7d-5f5fcde472d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e044b7d5-8486-58d6-b3fe-085072e21840" :answer/id #uuid "e044b7d5-8486-58d6-b3fe-085072e21840" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5d698685-38f5-5e4a-b709-e155fb9c6b96" :question/id #uuid "5d698685-38f5-5e4a-b709-e155fb9c6b96" :question/math-academy-id "q-14379" :question/problem "The point $P(-21,17)$ is acted on by a shift of $7$ units down followed by reflection across the line $y=x.$ What is the image of $P$ under this transformation?" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the functional representations of our two transformations:

- A shift of $7$ units down can be represented by the function 

$$
(x,y)↦(x,y-7).
$$

- A reflection across the line $y=x$ can be represented by the function

$$
(x,y)↦(y,x).
$$

Let's apply the given transformations to the point $P$ using our functions:

First, we apply the shift. The image of the point $(-21,17)$ under the shift is

$$
(-21,17)↦(-21,17-7)=(-21,10).
$$



Then, we apply the reflection. The image of the point $(-21,10)$ under the reflection is

$$
(-21,10)↦(10,-21).
$$

Therefore, the resulting point is $(10,-21).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a4faa69a-a341-53a6-a6fc-1d912a96ca49"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a4faa69a-a341-53a6-a6fc-1d912a96ca49" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4faa69a-a341-53a6-a6fc-1d912a96ca49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76be68a4-09fd-5e88-831d-5a29033970e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e4fd129a-3897-566f-b017-d5935d9fe3c3" "answer-0a8dfe3f-027c-5611-b8c1-25544135099d" "answer-fa18dc99-0972-5734-8b7c-acec22695fad" "answer-76be68a4-09fd-5e88-831d-5a29033970e7" "answer-26c21e0c-194c-582e-8fc4-220401ac3b5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4fd129a-3897-566f-b017-d5935d9fe3c3" :answer/id #uuid "e4fd129a-3897-566f-b017-d5935d9fe3c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-10,-21)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a8dfe3f-027c-5611-b8c1-25544135099d" :answer/id #uuid "0a8dfe3f-027c-5611-b8c1-25544135099d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-21,-10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa18dc99-0972-5734-8b7c-acec22695fad" :answer/id #uuid "fa18dc99-0972-5734-8b7c-acec22695fad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-21,10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76be68a4-09fd-5e88-831d-5a29033970e7" :answer/id #uuid "76be68a4-09fd-5e88-831d-5a29033970e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(10,-21)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26c21e0c-194c-582e-8fc4-220401ac3b5f" :answer/id #uuid "26c21e0c-194c-582e-8fc4-220401ac3b5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(21,-10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ba81a168-e077-501b-a6b1-f0f2d8fe936c" :question/id #uuid "ba81a168-e077-501b-a6b1-f0f2d8fe936c" :question/math-academy-id "q-45446" :question/problem "![](images/28/28c680b8b528eb436ec1f4ed94bb49393110bc1275e077b9ee170704172024a7.p