Calculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is

$$
\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\overset{―}{y}).\end{aligned}
$$

First, we calculate the sample means $\overset{―}{x}$ and $\overset{―}{y}:$

$$
\overset{―}{x}=\frac{1.2+1.0+0.7+1.3+1.8+1.4+1.7}{7}=1.3
$$

$$
\overset{―}{y}=\frac{6.6+6.1+5.7+6.0+6.3+5.9+5.4}{7}=6
$$

Next, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.

| **$\,{x}_{i}\,$** | $1.2$ | $1.0$ | $0.7$ | $1.3$ | $1.8$ | $1.7$ | $1.4$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **$\,{y}_{i}\,$** | $6.6$ | $6.1$ | $5.7$ | $6.0$ | $6.3$ | $5.9$ | $5.4$ |
| **$\,({x}_{i}-\overset{―}{x})\,$** | $-0.1$ | $-0.3$ | $-0.6$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ |
| **$\,({y}_{i}-\overset{―}{y})\,$** | $0.6$ | $0.1$ | $-0.3$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $-0.1$ | $-0.6$ |
| **$\,({x}_{i}-\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\overset{―}{y})\,$** | $-0.06$ | $-0.03$ | $0.18$ | $0$ | $0.15$ | $-0.04$ | $-0.06$ |

