27-5624-995c-489290485c6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128027" :question/problem "Find the value of $(-\frac{12}{5})÷(-3).$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a negative number by a negative number gives a positive number. Hence, the result will be positive.

Therefore, since 

$$
\frac{12}{5}÷3=\frac{12}{5\times 3}=\frac{12}{15}=\frac{4}{5},
$$

we obtain

$$
(-\frac{12}{5})÷(-3)=\frac{4}{5}.
$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4b9b6de2-c942-5b7d-bee5-f32a9154bfcb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b9b6de2-c942-5b7d-bee5-f32a9154bfcb" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b9b6de2-c942-5b7d-bee5-f32a9154bfcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-31fe9d50-00ed-566e-af8a-d1bb3e363580" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92639e1b-9c28-54c1-b941-f73ffe10bfb2" "answer-ae9d109d-0856-50b3-91be-dcbd5c513945" "answer-cb0bbf4b-84c5-5b4b-bf9f-be7a1d428368" "answer-31fe9d50-00ed-566e-af8a-d1bb3e363580" "answer-055df541-ba49-5b08-8eb5-364df6d7f59e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92639e1b-9c28-54c1-b941-f73ffe10bfb2" :answer/id #uuid "92639e1b-9c28-54c1-b941-f73ffe10bfb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae9d109d-0856-50b3-91be-dcbd5c513945" :answer/id #uuid "ae9d109d-0856-50b3-91be-dcbd5c513945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb0bbf4b-84c5-5b4b-bf9f-be7a1d428368" :answer/id #uuid "cb0bbf4b-84c5-5b4b-bf9f-be7a1d428368" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31fe9d50-00ed-566e-af8a-d1bb3e363580" :answer/id #uuid "31fe9d50-00ed-566e-af8a-d1bb3e363580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-055df541-ba49-5b08-8eb5-364df6d7f59e" :answer/id #uuid "055df541-ba49-5b08-8eb5-364df6d7f59e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110776 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d513115b-ad74-5e72-8ee2-71bd9f120a6f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d513115b-ad74-5e72-8ee2-71bd9f120a6f" :question/id #uuid "d513115b-ad74-5e72-8ee2-71bd9f120a6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128174" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f18036ac5790bda530116c6847243108f9617f9ae12fcbc5c1b2c3fff018985.png)

Which of the following terms describe the shape above?

I. Parallelogram

II. Rectangle

III. Rhombus" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.

![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)

Let's now look at the terms one by one.

- The given figure is a quadrilateral with two pairs of opposite congruent sides, so it is a parallelogram.

- Since the four angles of the quadrilateral are right angles, it is a rectangle.

- The given figure is a quadrilateral where the sides are not all congruent. So it is **not** a rhombus.

Consequently, the given shape is described by terms I (parallelogram), and II (rectangle)." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-27071654-a089-55fa-816c-6ef4bea74f2e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27071654-a089-55fa-816c-6ef4bea74f2e" :answer-field/id #uuid "27071654-a089-55fa-816c-6ef4bea74f2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-756c1651-49c5-59b4-9237-64c638bfd4f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-756c1651-49c5-59b4-9237-64c638bfd4f1" "answer-0099a153-14ac-5228-adff-948144c7c511" "answer-164cdbc6-b14e-5459-8e4d-4f24d14ceda3" "answer-eb7b757c-1895-5c25-80ab-64cfd132b5b7" "answer-19ac550c-b465-5b11-ae37-62b736f5ff29"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-756c1651-49c5-59b4-9237-64c638bfd4f1" :answer/id #uuid "756c1651-49c5-59b4-9237-64c638bfd4f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0099a153-14ac-5228-adff-948144c7c511" :answer/id #uuid "0099a153-14ac-5228-adff-948144c7c511" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-164cdbc6-b14e-5459-8e4d-4f24d14ceda3" :answer/id #uuid "164cdbc6-b14e-5459-8e4d-4f24d14ceda3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb7b757c-1895-5c25-80ab-64cfd132b5b7" :answer/id #uuid "eb7b757c-1895-5c25-80ab-64cfd132b5b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19ac550c-b465-5b11-ae37-62b736f5ff29" :answer/id #uuid "19ac550c-b465-5b11-ae37-62b736f5ff29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138511 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8e8a0eda-6609-511f-9732-1a6312007048"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e8a0eda-6609-511f-9732-1a6312007048" :question/id #uuid "8e8a0eda-6609-511f-9732-1a6312007048" :question/math-academy-id "q-175581" :question/problem "$\frac{2}{5}x+4y+\frac{5}{2}x+3y=${{field-1}}
$x\,+$
{{field-2}}
$y$" :question/worked-solution "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{2}{5}x+4y+\frac{5}{2}x+3y & = \\ (\frac{2}{5}x+\frac{5}{2}x)+(4y+3y) & = \\ (\frac{2}{5}+\frac{5}{2})x+(4+3)y & = \\ (\frac{4}{10}+\frac{25}{10})x+7y & = \\ (\frac{4+25}{10})x+7y & = \\ \frac{29}{10}\,x+7\,y\end{aligned}
$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cebc456f-ee3c-58cf-96e7-c237efa764f7" "answer-field-aa265d47-40f3-5a3f-9bf0-25685f2be3fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cebc456f-ee3c-58cf-96e7-c237efa764f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "cebc456f-ee3c-58cf-96e7-c237efa764f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6ee09fa0-6224-5178-b8f9-36c108594771" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ee09fa0-6224-5178-b8f9-36c108594771"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ee09fa0-6224-5178-b8f9-36c108594771" :answer/id #uuid "6ee09fa0-6224-5178-b8f9-36c108594771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\frac{29}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aa265d47-40f3-5a3f-9bf0-25685f2be3fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa265d47-40f3-5a3f-9bf0-25685f2be3fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7dda24c2-846e-5ae5-9e55-258b14393706" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7dda24c2-846e-5ae5-9e55-258b14393706"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dda24c2-846e-5ae5-9e55-258b14393706" :answer/id #uuid "7dda24c2-846e-5ae5-9e55-258b14393706" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064258 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f3e4db00-9ed0-5e91-8213-2ca14aefffbb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3e4db00-9ed0-5e91-8213-2ca14aefffbb" :question/id #uuid "f3e4db00-9ed0-5e91-8213-2ca14aefffbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103625" :question/problem "If $\frac{5x-10y-2z}{5}$ is written in the form $ax+by+cz,$ what are the values of  $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{5x-10y-2z}{5} & = \\ \frac{5x}{5}-\frac{10y}{5}-\frac{2z}{5} & = \\ \frac{5}{5}\cdot x-\frac{10}{5}\cdot y-\frac{2}{5}\cdot z & = \\ 1\cdot x-2\cdot y-\frac{2}{5}\cdot z & = \\ x-2y-\frac{2z}{5} & .\end{aligned}
$$

Writing the above in the form $ax+by+cz,$ we get

$$
\begin{aligned}{{(1)}_{⏟}}_{a}x+{{(-2)}_{⏟}}_{b}y+{{(-\frac{2}{5})}_{⏟}}_{c}z.\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore,  $a=1,$ $b=-2$ and $c=-\frac{2}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9ac144df-2131-57c9-bfbb-43bd44e355e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ac144df-2131-57c9-bfbb-43bd44e355e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac144df-2131-57c9-bfbb-43bd44e355e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fc3e3b6b-5c5d-5998-9365-602913fed818" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc3e3b6b-5c5d-5998-9365-602913fed818" "answer-86d1e6a6-32cc-5370-9d0c-04db2526ab57" "answer-bd7d356d-5fef-5042-be30-4689b4b9777a" "answer-2385595f-7f7d-5bcb-b6db-b0de1f32a65b" "answer-5bd91c40-af18-5c9d-b794-20c583df8cb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc3e3b6b-5c5d-5998-9365-602913fed818" :answer/id #uuid "fc3e3b6b-5c5d-5998-9365-602913fed818" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=-2$ and $c=-\frac{2}{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86d1e6a6-32cc-5370-9d0c-04db2526ab57" :answer/id #uuid "86d1e6a6-32cc-5370-9d0c-04db2526ab57" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=-2$ and $c=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd7d356d-5fef-5042-be30-4689b4b9777a" :answer/id #uuid "bd7d356d-5fef-5042-be30-4689b4b9777a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=\frac{1}{5}$ and $c=-\frac{2}{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2385595f-7f7d-5bcb-b6db-b0de1f32a65b" :answer/id #uuid "2385595f-7f7d-5bcb-b6db-b0de1f32a65b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=2,$ $b=-2$ and $c=-1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bd91c40-af18-5c9d-b794-20c583df8cb8" :answer/id #uuid "5bd91c40-af18-5c9d-b794-20c583df8cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=\frac{1}{5},$ $b=2$ and $c=\frac{2}{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138537 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8a9682b8-c5c3-5a53-a91f-bba592503325"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-poin