$)^{3}\cdot \frac{3}{n}]$" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as

$$
{\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\text{d}x={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\cdot Δx,
$$

where $Δx=\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$

In the definite integral

$$
{\int }_{1}^{4}3{x}^{3}\,\text{d}x,
$$

the function is $f(x)=3{x}^{3},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have

$$
Δx=\frac{4-1}{n}=\frac{3}{n},
$$

and therefore

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{1}^{4}3{x}^{3}\,\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\cdot Δx \\  & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\cdot \frac{3}{n})\cdot \frac{3}{n}] \\  & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[3{(\,1+\frac{3i}{n}\,)}^{3}\cdot \frac{3}{n}].\end{aligned}
$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d7e966e-716c-5603-9e5c-a619cf8a9b2c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d7e966e-716c-5603-9e5c-a619cf8a9b2c" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7e966e-716c-5603-9e5c-a619cf8a9b2c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ea371c3a-ee29-5549-a033-ba24d614dda7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ea371c3a-ee29-5549-a033-ba24d614dda7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea371c3a-ee29-5549-a033-ba24d614dda7" :answer/id #uuid "ea371c3a-ee29-5549-a033-ba24d614dda7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\frac{3i}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-328da786-31ee-5734-9605-611059a862b9" :question/id #uuid "328da786-31ee-5734-9605-611059a862b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-346178" :question/problem "Express ${\int }_{1}^{7}\frac{2}{x+3}\,\text{d}x$ as the limit of a left Riemann sum.

