$$"] ["question-fe245032-d155-5a02-8475-f1836177bbab" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a" :answer-field/id #uuid "da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a"] ["answer-4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a" :answer/id #uuid "4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a"] ["answer-4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a" :answer/value "\frac{6j}{n}-1"] ["answer-field-da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a" :answer-field/correct "answer-4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a"] ["answer-field-da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a" :answer-field/choices "answer-4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a"] ["question-fe245032-d155-5a02-8475-f1836177bbab" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a"] [17592186096629 :knowledge-point/questions "question-fe245032-d155-5a02-8475-f1836177bbab"] ["question-21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684" :question/id #uuid "21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684"] ["question-21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684" :question/math-academy-id "q-116626"] ["question-21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\sqrt{x+2}$ between $x=-2$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $7$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?"] ["question-21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   

$$
{\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,
$$

where ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\frac{b-a}{n}.$ 

We're told that there are $n=7$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=2.$ So, the step size is

$$
