wer-242d5a8d-320a-55dd-af45-50bb63662fa4"] ["answer-field-4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9" :answer-field/choices "answer-16912225-3f70-5541-b574-3061e2e7b38e"] ["answer-field-4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9" :answer-field/choices "answer-761dcd9a-706c-5db6-a6b8-883ea8047a63"] ["answer-field-4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9" :answer-field/choices "answer-9b62e5a4-9e97-5400-851f-d6ea027be307"] ["answer-field-4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9" :answer-field/choices "answer-242d5a8d-320a-55dd-af45-50bb63662fa4"] ["answer-field-4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9" :answer-field/choices "answer-e1d1bf4f-0539-5436-aeaf-4b61a267639b"] ["question-3994f797-7a6e-5428-aacb-fe36a9051f76" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9"] [17592186096629 :knowledge-point/questions "question-3994f797-7a6e-5428-aacb-fe36a9051f76"] [17592186096850 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0] ["question-b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/id #uuid "b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0"] ["question-b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-138608"] ["question-b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/problem "$$
X=[\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3 \\ 7 & 5 & 9\end{aligned}]
$$

Consider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$"] ["question-b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix

$$
X=[\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\ | & | &  & |\end{aligned}]
$$

is given by 

$$
B=[\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\ | & | &  & |\end{aligned}]
$$

where ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.

From the matrix, we have that  

$$
{x}_{1}=[\begin{aligned}2 \\ 7\end{aligned}],\,{x}_{2}=[\begin{aligned}-2 \\ 5\end{aligned}],\,{x}_{3}=[\begin{aligned}3 \\ 9\end{aligned}].
$$

As a result, the sample mean is

$$
\begin{aligned}m & =\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\  & =\frac{1}{3}([\begin{aligned}2 \\ 7\end{aligned}]+[\begin{aligned}-2 \\ 5\end{aligned}]+[\begin{aligned}3 \\ 9\end{aligned}]) \\  & =\frac{1}{3}[\begin{aligned}3 \\ 21\end{aligned}] \\  & =[\begin{aligned}1 \\ 7\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we have the following:

$$
\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\begin{aligned}2 \\ 7\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}1 \\ 7\end{aligned}]=[\begin{aligned}1 \\ 0\end{aligned}] \\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\begin{aligned}-2 \\ 5\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}1 \\ 7\end{aligned}]=[\begin{aligned}-3 \\ -2\end{aligned}] \\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\begin{aligned}3 \\ 9\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}1 \\ 7\end{aligned}]=[\begin{aligned}2 \\ 2\end{aligned}]\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore,  the mean-deviation form is

$$
B=[\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\ 0 & -2 & 2\end{aligned}].
