- Next, we take $\overline{A'B'}$ and shift it by $3$ units down. This gives the segment $\overline{A''B''}\mathbin{:}$

![](images/a7/a78807d3f1fb43f3773671f7c4f5696dd3779ae9ce1d8da797377c3574170a92.png)"] [17592186073920 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0] [17592186055516 :question/problem "Calculate ${log}_{9}⁡(27)$ without using a calculator."] [17592186055516 :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:

$$
{log}_{a}⁡X=\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}
$$

In our case, $a=9,$ and $X=27.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $3,$ we set $b=3.$ So, we have:

$$
\begin{aligned}{log}_{9}⁡(27) & =\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(27)}{{log}_{3}⁡(9)} \\  & =\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({3}^{3})}{{log}_{3}⁡({3}^{2})} \\  & =\frac{3}{2}\end{aligned}
$$"] [17592186055516 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186054333 :answer-field/correct 17592186054334] ["question-da9958bc-8f70-50e7-9f99-fa451b16875b" :question/id #uuid "da9958bc-8f70-50e7-9f99-fa451b16875b"] ["question-da9958bc-8f70-50e7-9f99-fa451b16875b" :question/math-academy-id "q-100672"] ["question-da9958bc-8f70-50e7-9f99-fa451b16875b" :question/problem "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{7}⁡(12)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places."] ["question-da9958bc-8f70-50e7-9f99-fa451b16875b" :question/worked-solution "Let's calculate ${log}_{7}⁡(12)$ by changing the base $7$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).

