$+\,⋯\,.$"] ["question-13fe64c0-baa0-5796-8788-eb725aaab3f7" :question/worked-solution "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is

$$
\begin{aligned}\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯\,.\end{aligned}
$$

Replacing $x$ with $2x$ in the above expansion and simplifying gives

$$
\begin{aligned}\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & =1-\frac{{(2x)}^{2}}{2!}+\frac{{(2x)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯ \\  & =1-\frac{4{x}^{2}}{2}+\frac{16{x}^{4}}{24}-⋯ \\  & =1-2{x}^{2}+\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4}-⋯\,.\end{aligned}
$$"] ["question-13fe64c0-baa0-5796-8788-eb725aaab3f7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-cedee66a-24e0-5438-81e1-9b1ee66ad818" :answer-field/id #uuid "cedee66a-24e0-5438-81e1-9b1ee66ad818"] ["answer-910fe9d5-713a-5711-820b-f8e6362219bd" :answer/id #uuid "910fe9d5-713a-5711-820b-f8e6362219bd"] ["answer-910fe9d5-713a-5711-820b-f8e6362219bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-910fe9d5-713a-5711-820b-f8e6362219bd" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-field-cedee66a-24e0-5438-81e1-9b1ee66ad818" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-cedee66a-24e0-5438-81e1-9b1ee66ad818" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-cedee66a-24e0-5438-81e1-9b1ee66ad818" :answer-field/correct "answer-910fe9d5-713a-5711-820b-f8e6362219bd"] ["answer-field-cedee66a-24e0-5438-81e1-9b1ee66ad818" :answer-field/choices "answer-910fe9d5-713a-5711-820b-f8e6362219bd"] ["answer-field-8524f743-235a-5ef1-b250-79c5edc9a5f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8524f743-235a-5ef1-b250-79c5edc9a5f1"] ["answer-460370c3-6fd1-58b4-af17-4ac1e539d948" :answer/id #uuid "460370c3-6fd1-58b4-af17-4ac1e539d948"] ["answer-460370c3-6fd1-58b4-af17-4ac1e539d948" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-460370c3-6fd1-58b4-af17-4ac1e539d948" :answer/value "-2x^{2}"] ["answer-field-8524f743-235a-5ef1-b250-79c5edc9a5f1" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-8524f743-235a-5ef1-b250-79c5edc9a5f1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-8524f743-235a-5ef1-b250-79c5edc9a5f1" :answer-field/correct "answer-460370c3-6fd1-58b4-af17-4ac1e539d948"] ["answer-field-8524f743-235a-5ef1-b250-79c5edc9a5f1" :answer-field/choices "answer-460370c3-6fd1-58b4-af17-4ac1e539d948"] ["answer-field-f190c321-fde6-5144-85cf-fd6b258c5583" :answer-field/id #uuid "f190c321-fde6-5144-85cf-fd6b258c5583"] ["answer-329ae851-0e7a-5282-99fd-555e056c7319" :answer/id #uuid "329ae851-0e7a-5282-99fd-555e056c7319"] ["answer-329ae851-0e7a-5282-99fd-555e056c7319" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-329ae851-0e7a-5282-99fd-555e056c7319" :answer/value "\frac{2}{3}x^{4}"] ["answer-field-f190c321-fde6-5144-85cf-fd6b258c5583" :answer-field/key "field-3"] ["answer-field-f190c321-fde6-5144-85cf-fd6b258c5583" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-f190c321-fde6-5144-85cf-fd6b258c5583" :answer-field/correct "answer-329ae851-0e7a-5282-99fd-555e056c7319"] ["answer-field-f190c321-fde6-5144-85cf-fd6b258c5583" :answer-field/choices "answer-329ae851-0e7a-5282-99fd-555e056c7319"] ["question-13fe64c0-baa0-5796-8788-eb725aaab3f7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-cedee66a-24e0-5438-81e1-9b1ee66ad818"] ["question-13fe64c0-baa0-5796-8788-eb725aaab3f7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-8524f743-235a-5ef1-b250-79c5edc9a5f1"] ["question-13fe64c0-baa0-5796-8788-eb725aaab3f7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f190c321-fde6-5144-85cf-fd6b258c5583"] [17592186087787 :knowledge-point/questions "question-13fe64c0-baa0-5796-8788-eb725aaab3f7"] ["question-151db205-6c32-596b-ad29-fa17f10dd215" :question/id #uuid "151db205-6c32-596b-ad29-fa17f10dd215"] ["question-151db205-6c32-596b-ad29-fa17f10dd215" :question/math-academy-id "q-129772"] ["question-151db205-6c32-596b-ad29-fa17f10dd215" :question/problem "Write the second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ about $x=0.$

${P}_{2}(x)\,=\,$
{{field-1}}"] ["question-151db205-6c32-596b-ad29-fa17f10dd215" :question/worked-solution "Previously, we found that the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=0$ is

$$
{P}_{3}(x)=2-\frac{1}{2}x+\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}
$$

and the Maclaurin series for $\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ is

$$
\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=1-2{x}^{2}+\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4}-⋯\,.
$$

To find the expansion of $f(x)\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),$ we multiply the expansions of $f(x)$ and $\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),$ as follows: 

$$
f(x)\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=(2-\frac{1}{2}x+\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3})(1-2{x}^{2}+\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4}-⋯)
$$

Let's work out each term individually:

* There is a constant term, given by

$$
2\cdot 1=2.
$$

* There is a single $x$ term, given by

$$
-\frac{1}{2}x\cdot 1=-\frac{1}{2}x.
$$

* There are two   ${x}^{2}$  terms and their sum is given by 

$$
\begin{aligned}2\cdot (-2{x}^{2})+\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}\cdot 1 & =-4{x}^{2}+\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}, \\  & =-\frac{15}{4}{x}^{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

All other terms contain powers of $x$ greater than $2.$

Therefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ about $x=0$ is

$$
\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =2-\frac{1}{2}x-\frac{15}{4}{x}^{2}.\end{aligned}
$$"] ["question-151db205-6c32-596b-ad29-fa17f10dd215" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-36a65f47-1d59-5158-bad0-5ab25b1d5439" :answer-field/id #uuid "36a65f47-1d59-5158-bad0-5ab25b1d5439"] ["answer-0a41fa7c-ff54-5e79-94c5-8f781a6e77ab" :answer/id #uuid "0a41fa7c-ff54-5e79-94c5-8f781a6e77ab"] ["answer-0a41fa7c-ff54-5e79-94c5-8f781a6e77ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0a41fa7c-ff54-5e79-94c5-8f781a6e77ab" :answer/value "2-\frac{1}{2}x-\frac{15}{4}x^{2}"] ["answer-field-36a65f47-1d59-5158-bad0-5ab25b1d5439" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-36a65f47-1d59-5158-bad0-5ab25b1d5439" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-36a65f47-1d59-5158-bad0-5ab25b1d5439" :answer-field/correct "answer-0a41fa7c-ff54-5e79-94c5-8f781a6e77ab"] ["answer-field-36a65f47-1d59-5158-bad0-5ab25b1d5439" :answer-field/choices "answer-0a41fa7c-ff54-5e79-94c5-8f781a6e77ab"] ["question-151db205-6c32-596b-ad29-fa17f10dd215" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-36a65f47-1d59-5158-bad0-5ab25b1d5439"] [17592186087790 :knowledge-point/questions "question-151db205-6c32-596b-ad29-fa17f10dd215"] ["question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a" :question/id #uuid "7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a"] ["question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129773"] ["question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a" :question/problem "Use the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ from part 2 to find the fourth-degree Taylor approximation of $g(x)$ about $x=0.$ Find $g(1)$ using this approximation.

$g(x)\,≈\,2x-\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}\,+\,$
{{field-1}}${x}^{3}$
$+$
{{field-2}}${x}^{4}$

$g(1)\,≈\,$
{{field-3}}"] ["question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a" :question/worked-solution "We have that

$$
f(x)≈{P}_{3}(x)=2-\frac{1}{2}x+\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}.
$$

Therefore, we can approximate $g(x)={\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t$ by integrating the above polynomial term-by-term, as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t \\  & ≈{\int }_{0}^{x}(2-\frac{1}{2}x+\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3})\text{d}t \\  & ={[2t-\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}+\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\frac{1}{24}{t}^{4}]}_{0}^{x} \\  & =[2x-\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+\frac{1}{12}{x}^{3}-\frac{1}{24}{x}^{4}]-0 \\  & =2x-\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+\frac{1}{12}{x}^{3}-\frac{1}{24}{x}^{4}\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we evaluate $g(1)$ using the approximation above:

$$
\begin{aligned}g(1) & ≈2(1)-\frac{1}{4}(1)^{2}+\frac{1}{12}(1)^{3}-\frac{1}{24}(1)^{4} \\  & =2-\frac{1}{4}+\frac{1}{12}-\frac{1}{24} \\  & =\frac{43}{24}\end{aligned}
$$"] ["question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-eca13d5a-0f01-5d47-ac43-fe2e58fa3861" :answer-field/id #uuid "eca13d5a-0f01-5d47-ac43-fe2e58fa3861"] ["answer-2bc6b863-cf8b-5177-8c7c-cac0897e6dcd" :answer/id #uuid "2bc6b863-cf8b-5177-8c7c-cac0897e6dcd"] ["answer-2bc6b863-cf8b-5177-8c7c-cac0897e6dcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2bc6b863-cf8b-5177-8c7c-cac0897e6dcd" :answer/value "\frac{1}{12}"] ["answer-field-eca13d5a-0f01-5d47-ac43-fe2e58fa3861" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-eca13d5a-0f01-5d47-ac43-fe2e58fa3861" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-eca13d5a-0f01-5d47-ac43-fe2e58fa3861" :answer-field/correct "answer-2bc6b863-cf8b-5177-8c7c-cac0897e6dcd"] ["answer-field-eca13d5a-0f01-5d47-ac43-fe2e58fa3861" :answer-field/choices "answer-2bc6b863-cf8b-5177-8c7c-cac0897e6dcd"] ["answer-field-63d4de25-9c00-54d0-adea-350732c1c21d" :answer-field/id #uuid "63d4de25-9c00-54d0-adea-350732c1c21d"] ["answer-37425270-d6a5-558f-b94a-d16bcf4ad148" :answer/id #uuid "37425270-d6a5-558f-b94a-d16bcf4ad148"] ["answer-37425270-d6a5-558f-b94a-d16bcf4ad148" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-37425270-d6a5-558f-b94a-d16bcf4ad148" :answer/value "-\frac{1}{24}"] ["answer-field-63d4de25-9c00-54d0-adea-350732c1c21d" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-63d4de25-9c00-54d0-adea-350732c1c21d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-63d4de25-9c00-54d0-adea-350732c1c21d" :answer-field/correct "answer-37425270-d6a5-558f-b94a-d16bcf4ad148"] ["answer-field-63d4de25-9c00-54d0-adea-350732c1c21d" :answer-field/choices "answer-37425270-d6a5-558f-b94a-d16bcf4ad148"] ["answer-field-33cb2526-ce60-5170-b71a-6d4b10c2625e" :answer-field/id #uuid "33cb2526-ce60-5170-b71a-6d4b10c2625e"] ["answer-69f4e2a8-d94d-54bf-b805-7fcfd592c5e8" :answer/id #uuid "69f4e2a8-d94d-54bf-b805-7fcfd592c5e8"] ["answer-69f4e2a8-d94d-54bf-b805-7fcfd592c5e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-69f4e2a8-d94d-54bf-b805-7fcfd592c5e8" :answer/value "\frac{43}{24}"] ["answer-field-33cb2526-ce60-5170-b71a-6d4b10c2625e" :answer-field/key "field-3"] ["answer-field-33cb2526-ce60-5170-b71a-6d4b10c2625e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-33cb2526-ce60-5170-b71a-6d4b10c2625e" :answer-field/correct "answer-69f4e2a8-d94d-54bf-b805-7fcfd592c5e8"] ["answer-field-33cb2526-ce60-5170-b71a-6d4b10c2625e" :answer-field/choices "answer-69f4e2a8-d94d-54bf-b805-7fcfd592c5e8"] ["question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-eca13d5a-0f01-5d47-ac43-fe2e58fa3861"] ["question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-63d4de25-9c00-54d0-adea-350732c1c21d"] ["question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-33cb2526-ce60-5170-b71a-6d4b10c2625e"] [17592186087794 :knowledge-point/questions "question-7baabd1b-d935-56aa-a7ed-5d322543486a"] ["question-2d7243f0-f25d-51c0-9680-07e1df8e0114" :question/id #uuid "2d7243f0-f25d-51c0-9680-07e1df8e0114"] ["question-2d7243f0-f25d-51c0-9680-07e1df8e0114" :question/math-academy-id "q-129774"] ["question-2d7243f0-f25d-51c0-9680-07e1df8e0114" :question/problem "Find the value of ${a}_{5},$ the fifth nonzero term of the alternating series $S={\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }{a}_{n}.$

${a}_{5}\,=\,$
{{field-1}}"] ["question-2d7243f0-f25d-51c0-9680-07e1df8e0114" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the terms of our series $S={\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }{a}_{n}$ are the coefficients of the Maclaurin series for $g(x).$

Previously, we found the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x):$

$$
f(x)≈{P}_{4}(x)=2-\frac{1}{2}x+\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}+\frac{1}{8}{x}^{4}
$$

To find the ${x}^{5}$ term of the Maclaurin series of $g(x),$ we simply need to integrate the ${x}^{4}$ term of ${P}_{4}(x):$

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{1}{8}{t}^{4}\,\text{d}x & =\frac{1}{8}{\int }_{0}^{x}{t}^{4}\,\text{d}x \\  & =\frac{1}{40}{t}^{5}\,{|}_{0}^{x} \\  & =\frac{1}{40}{x}^{5}\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, ${a}_{5}$ is the coefficient of $\frac{1}{40}{x}^{5},$ that is, ${a}_{5}=\frac{1}{40}.$"] ["question-2d7243f0-f25d-51c0-9680-07e1df8e0114" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b0e904c0-c52c-57be-803f-4a9e12590679" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0e904c0-c52c-57be-803f-4a9e12590679"] ["answer-52ceb76e-e2b2-5e97-834d-102232989a20" :answer/id #uuid "52ceb76e-e2b2-5e97-834d-102232989a20"] ["answer-52ceb76e-e2b2-5e97-834d-102232989a20" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-52ceb76e-e2b2-5e97-834d-102232989a20" :answer/value "\frac{1}{40}"] ["answer-field-b0e904c0-c52c-57be-803f-4a9e12590679" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b0e904c0-c52c-57be-803f-4a9e12590679" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b0e904c0-c52c-57be-803f-4a9e12590679" :answer-field/correct "answer-52ceb76e-e2b2-5e97-834d-102232989a20"] ["answer-field-b0e904c0-c52c-57be-803f-4a9e12590679" :answer-field/choices "answer-52ceb76e-e2b2-5e97-834d-102232989a20"] ["question-2d7243f0-f25d-51c0-9680-07e1df8e0114" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b0e904c0-c52c-57be-803f-4a9e12590679"] [17592186064196 :knowledge-point/questions "question-2d7243f0-f25d-51c0-9680-07e1df8e0114"] ["question-0fac5cd1-6321-5b31-b6c2-3285240579dd" :question/id #uuid "0fac5cd1-6321-5b31-b6c2-3285240579dd"] ["question-0fac5cd1-6321-5b31-b6c2-3285240579dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-129775"] ["question-0fac5cd1-6321-5b31-b6c2-3285240579dd" :question/problem "Let $a$ denote the approximation of $g(1)$ found in part 5. According to the alternating series error bound, we have that 

$$
|g(1)-a|<k
$$

 for some real number $k.$ Find the value of $k.$

$k\,=\,$
{{field-1}}"] ["question-0fac5cd1-6321-5b31-b6c2-3285240579dd" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $g(1)$ represents the sum of the convergent alternating series, while the approximation $a$ represents the fourth partial sum of this series:

$$
g(1)=S={\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }{a}_{n},\,a={s}_{4}
$$

As a result, 

$$
|g(1)-a|=|S-{s}_{4}|.
$$

We also know that ${a}_{5}=\frac{1}{40}.$ Therefore, according to the alternating series error bound, we obtain that

$$
\begin{aligned}|S-{s}_{4}| & <|{a}_{5}| \\  & =|\frac{1}{40}| \\  & =\frac{1}{40}.\end{aligned}
$$"] ["question-0fac5cd1-6321-5b31-b6c2-3285240579dd" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-ab037cff-04b7-568a-b9a5-76d4f84d88cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab037cff-04b7-568a-b9a5-76d4f84d88cb"] ["answer-a1aef4d3-779b-5ba2-a634-7ad64802dc9d" :answer/id #uuid "a1aef4d3-779b-5ba2-a634-7ad64802dc9d"] ["answer-a1aef4d3-779b-5ba2-a634-7ad64802dc9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a1aef4d3-779b-5ba2-a634-7ad64802dc9d" :answer/value "\frac{1}{40}"] ["answer-field-ab037cff-04b7-568a-b9a5-76d4f84d88cb" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-ab037cff-04b7-568a-b9a5-76d4f84d88cb" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-ab037cff-04b7-568a-b9a5-76d4f84d88cb" :answer-field/correct "answer-a1aef4d3-779b-5ba2-a634-7ad64802dc9d"] ["answer-field-ab037cff-04b7-568a-b9a5-76d4f84d88cb" :answer-field/choices "answer-a1aef4d3-779b-5ba2-a634-7ad64802dc9d"] ["question-0fac5cd1-6321-5b31-b6c2-3285240579dd" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ab037cff-04b7-568a-b9a5-76d4f84d88cb"] [17592186100924 :knowledge-point/questions "question-0fac5cd1-6321-5b31-b6c2-3285240579dd"] ["multistep-2175db54-7935-51ff-8029-dacec9980dc4" :multistep/id #uuid "2175db54-7935-51ff-8029-dacec9980dc4"] ["step-2c34a7a0-14a6-5a48-8af3-6b82adf7a7b5" :step/id #uuid "2c34a7a0-14a6-5a48-8af3-6b82adf7a7b5"] ["step-31a6c27d-2709-5a68-b854-2de759080b64" :step/id #uuid "31a6c27d-2709-5a68-b854-2de759080b64"] ["step-832556fe-efc8-5ab8-9e8b-358e94d12924" :step/id #uuid "832556fe-efc8-5ab8-9e8b-358e94d12924"] ["step-f8d97e8c-19ea-592c-b125-01880e771cd9" :step/id #uuid "f8d97e8c-19ea-592c-b125-01880e771cd9"] ["step-daf2b994-9ede-50c2-b149-3eac44f27ffa" :step/id #uuid "daf2b994-9ede-50c2-b149-3eac44f27ffa"] ["step-8633e111-13c5-5099-9481-a055364781f0" :step/id #uuid "8633e111-13c5-5099-9481-a055364781f0"] ["step-259f7312-1450-5437-8b0c-e3169741fe4f" :step/id #uuid "259f7312-1450-5437-8b0c-e3169741fe4f"] ["step-2c34a7a0-14a6-5a48-8af3-6b82adf7a7b5" :step/content "question-8