|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |"] ["question-133450b7-1b39-5639-acd0-5a1f9b4407fc" :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=4x-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=2$ and $x=4.$

This can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=4x-{x}^{2}$ between the lower limit $x=2$ and the upper limit $x=4,$ as follows:

