$$
{\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\,\text{d}x={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\cdot Δx
$$

where $Δx=\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$

Notice that we're given that the lower limit $a=-1.$ 

Comparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\frac{3}{n}.$ Therefore, 

$$
\frac{3}{n}=\frac{b-(-1)}{n}\,⟹\,b=2.
$$

Consequently, ${x}_{k}=-1+\frac{3k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=({x}_{k}+8)^{1/3}.$

Hence,

$$
{\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+8)^{1/3}\,\text{d}x={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{((-1+\frac{3k}{n})+8)}^{1/3}\cdot \frac{3}{n}].
$$

Therefore, the correct answer is 

$$
f(x)=(x+8)^{1/3}\,\text{and}\,b=2.
$$"] ["answer-f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2" :answer/id #uuid "f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2"] ["answer-f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2" :answer/value "e^x"] [17592186232563 :answer-field/correct "answer-f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2"] [17592186232563 :answer-field/choices "answer-f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2"] ["question-94a24590-9d5e-597a-b9fc-4e27a31e8bcf" :question/id #uuid "94a24590-9d5e-597a-b9fc-4e27a31e8bcf"] ["question-94a24590-9d5e-597a-b9fc-4e27a31e8bcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-346215"] ["question-94a24590-9d5e-597a-b9fc-4e27a31e8bcf" :question/problem "What is ${\int }_{1}^{4}(x+8)^{1/3}\,\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?

