Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{2}^{5}8{x}^{4}\,\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\cdot Δx \\  & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(2+i\cdot \frac{3}{n})\cdot \frac{3}{n}] \\  & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(2+\frac{3i}{n})\cdot \frac{3}{n}] \\  & ={lim}_{n\to \infty }{\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[8{(\,2+\frac{3i}{n}\,)}^{\,4}\cdot \frac{3}{n}].\end{aligned}
$$"] ["question-3c8de7d3-85f5-5987-bc43-0d9881c2dbaf" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3"] ["answer-d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e" :answer/id #uuid "d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e"] ["answer-d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e" :answer/value "2+\frac{3i}{n}"] ["answer-field-b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3" :answer-field/correct "answer-d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e"] ["answer-field-b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3" :answer-field/choices "answer-d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e"] ["question-3c8de7d3-85f5-5987-bc43-0d9881c2dbaf" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3"] [17592186096633 :knowledge-point/questions "question-3c8de7d3-85f5-5987-bc43-0d9881c2dbaf"] [17592186180025 :question/problem "If ${\int }_{C}z\,\text{d}x+x\,\text{d}y+y\,\text{d}z$ is equivalent to ${\int }_{C}F\cdot \text{d}r$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$"] [17592186180025 :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field 

$$
F(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\,i+Q(x,y,z)\,j+R(x,y,z)\,k
$$

defined on $C,$ we have

$$
{\int }_{C}F\cdot \text{d}r={\int }_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y+R\,\text{d}z
